  <!-- EN: soybean plant -->
  <RF_Soybean.label>大豆植物</RF_Soybean.label>
  <!-- EN: Soybeans play a central role in Japanese cuisine and its seasonings, making it a valuable source of vegetable protein for vegetarians. Soybeans are also used as a raw material for soy sauce. -->
  <RF_Soybean.description>大豆在日本料理及其调味料中扮演着核心角色，是素食者宝贵的植物蛋白来源。大豆也是酱油的原料。</RF_Soybean.description>
  <!-- EN: wasabi plant -->
  <RF_Wasabi.label>芥末植物</RF_Wasabi.label>
  <!-- EN: Wasabi is a cruciferous plant native to Japan. It grows in mountain streams and swamps and blooms white florets in spring. Rhizome and leaves are edible, but they are used as condiment and seasonings because of their strong pungent taste.\nNot grow on less fertile ground. -->
  <RF_Wasabi.description>山葵是一种原产于日本十字花科植物。它生长在山间溪流和沼泽中，春季会开出白色小花。其根茎和叶子均可食用，但因其味道辛辣刺鼻，通常被用作调味料和佐料。
不适合在贫瘠的土壤中种植。</RF_Wasabi.description>
